Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 01:02:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?perf(manager):=20server-driven=20overtake-tool?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20remote=20UI=20=E2=80=94=20coalesced,=20rev-gated=20poll?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The overtake-tool remote UI (Tool tab) was refreshed by each browser polling
independently via "refetch_tool", which had three problems on the shared shm
param channel that also serves the realtime audio/MIDI path:

1. Busy-escalation: handleRefetchTool read the cheap "rui_poll" digest with
   TryGetParam, but treated its mutex-busy return (ok=false) the same as an
   unsupported key and fell back to the expensive full "state" read. So under
   any contention (a concurrent SetParam, another tab, a preset resend) it did
   the heaviest possible read — defeating the rev-gate exactly when the channel
   was busiest, and self-amplifying under load.
2. No coalescing: N Tool-tab clients (main tab + pop-out) each triggered their
   own full "state" snapshot read on every rev change — N x the RT-adjacent cost.
3. No unload signal: when the overtake tool was unloaded the Tool tab kept
   polling a dead module forever and never cleared its iframe.

Replace the per-client browser poll with a single server-side toolTickLoop:
- reads "rui_poll" once per tick; on mutex-busy it SKIPS (never escalates);
- on a rev change does ONE "state" read fanned out to every stale client;
- otherwise pushes only the moving playhead;
- signals tool_info(gone) once when the tool unloads;
- adapts cadence (~100ms active / 400ms idle / 500ms no clients) so device->
  browser sync is tighter than the old 150-500ms browser poll without raising
  steady-state shm traffic.

handleRefetchTool becomes a no-op (kept so older browsers' timer messages don't
error). Per-client rev/tick cursors are now touched only by the ticker, guarded
by c.mu. Also: fetchAllParams now logs when a component's "state" snapshot
truncates at the 64KB param cap (invalid JSON is otherwise silently dropped and
the remote UI mysteriously stops refreshing).

Generic across all overtake tools — no module-specific assumptions; a tool that
predates the rui_poll digest still works via the coalesced full-fetch path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
